  <item>
    <title>06.《盐的代价/卡罗尔》文本细读：我不想在没有完全了解你之前就死去，你也有这种感觉吗，Carol？</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/6785a32c1bf3f0ab2bed5a36</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">6785a32c1bf3f0ab2bed5a36</guid>
    <pubDate>Tue, 14 Jan 2025 00:18:55 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>微博：她们_之间（下划线）</span></p><span></span><p><span>小红书/公众号：给陌生人看的日记本</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="0">00:00</a> Intro</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="22">00:22</a> 上期内容回顾</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="55">00:55</a> 第十一章开始的对话</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="213">03:33</a> Therese情书里提到的音乐</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="351">05:51</a> 女仆Florence 第一次出场</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="402">06:42</a> 导演Todd Haynes：每个爱情故事都是一个侦探小说</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="480">08:00</a> Carol和Therese关于旅行的对话</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="736">12:16</a> 关于Carol女儿Rindy：Carol不可能爱任何人超过Rindy了，Therese想</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="859">14:19</a> Carol谈论自己的婚姻：丈夫的家庭不接纳任何有自我主张的人</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1155">19:15</a> “我是丈夫买回家的一张挂毯”</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1330">22:10</a> 战争，商业阴谋，资本主义社会和《盐的代价》这本爱情小说有什么关系？</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1603">26:43</a> “我不想在没有完全了解你之前就死去，你也有这种感觉吗，Carol？”</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1647">27:27</a> Therese和Carol的对话不仅仅是情侣之间，还是两代女性之间的对话</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1743">29:03</a> 谈话从大的社会话题回到两个人的亲密关系</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="1926">32:06</a> 《盐的代价》这本书的“主题曲”：Embraceable You</span></p><span></span><p><span>（配乐版本是Sarah Vaughan - Embraceable You (EmArcy Records 1954)</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2123">35:23</a> 和Abby的交锋以宣告胜利结束</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="2498">41:38</a> “我可以给你一个晚安吻吗”</span></p><span></span><p><span>提到的论文：</span></p><span></span><p><span>Hesford, Victoria. “Patriotic Perversions: Patricia Highsmith’s Queer Vision of Cold War America in ‘The Price of Salt’, ‘The Blunderer’, and ‘Deep Water.’” </span><em><span>Women’s Studies Quarterly</span></em><span> 33, no. 3/4 (2005): 215–33.</span></p>]]></description>
